cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "areaFluForecast: neighborhood-scale influenza forecasting for public health departments"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A Python package that gives public health departments 1-4 week influenza
  forecasts for neighborhoods, ZIP codes or districts from their own weekly
  rates and area boundaries. It trains a spatio-temporal graph neural network,
  a tuned LSTM and Cola-GNN, checks each against persistence on the
  department's own past seasons before reporting forecasts, and gives
  calibrated FluSight-style quantiles. Pretrained Boston models support cities
  with short histories.
authors:
  - family-names: Biggs
    given-names: Mateo
    email: biggs.m@northeastern.edu
    affiliation: Northeastern University
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
# The concept DOI: resolves to the latest version on Zenodo.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23327109
repository-code: "https://github.com/CodeMateo15/areaFluForecast"
url: "https://areafluforecast.readthedocs.io"
keywords:
  - influenza
  - forecasting
  - graph neural network
  - public health
  - epidemiology
